                <pb facs="0518" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Netherlands/60: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Emmet</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-05-21T12:00:00-04:00">May 21,
                            1936—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>9. Legation’s despatch No. 403 of April 18. Please submit immediate telegraphic
                    report on present status of Government’s proposed legislation to prevent
                    fraudulent exportation to the United States of alcohol from the Netherlands. Do
                    you perceive any objection to our notifying Belgian Government that such
                    legislation is contemplated as a means of persuading the latter to do
                    likewise?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
